|\ISS LINUX Bootstrap
________________________________________________________________________________

Sabotage-style bootstrap for KISS Linux.

This allows building a KISS system from a regular host Linux distribution
without relying on a pre-built rootfs tarball.

Inspiration: sabotage-linux, kiss-llvm (@ packages), firasuke/mussel,
kiss-community/maintainer-utils.

Usage
________________________________________________________________________________

From a host with gcc, make, git, wget, etc.:

$ cd bootstrap
$ ./scripts/build-stage0 /path/to/rootfs

This builds a minimal stage0 (busybox, musl, binutils, gcc, make, kiss, ...)
using the host toolchain into the given directory.

Then:

$ ./scripts/enter-chroot /path/to/rootfs

Inside the chroot, set KISS_PATH and rebuild packages with the new toolchain
for a self-hosted system.

@-prefixed packages
________________________________________________________________________________

@stage0     Meta-package listing the minimal bootstrap set.
@toolchain  Staged toolchain build (musl headers -> binutils -> gcc -> musl).

These can be used once kiss is available in the environment.
